<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f7f7f8" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content={siteName} />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content={title} />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content={description} />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Xanh+Mono:ital@0;1&display=swap"
    />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/favicon-32.png" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href="/favicon-16.png" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="/apple-touch-icon.png" />
    <style is:global>
      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
      }

      html {
        background: #f7f7f8;
      }

      body {
        position: relative;
        min-height: 100vh;
        padding: 40px;
        color: #111111;
        /* Transparent so the backdrop below is not painted over. */
        background: transparent;
        font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, "Cascadia Mono",
          Consolas, "Liberation Mono", monospace;
        font-size: 12px;
        line-height: 20px;
      }

      /* Backdrop: the palace sits off to the right, and the page colour is
         washed over it from the left so the letter stays on clean paper. */
      body::before {
        content: "";
        position: fixed;
        inset: 0;
        z-index: -1;
        /* Stops are in pixels, not percentages: the letter is a fixed ~575px
           column, so a percentage stop drifts off it as the window widens.
           Hold the wash over the text, then let it dissolve slowly. */
        background-image: linear-gradient(
            to right,
            rgba(247, 247, 248, 0.97) 0,
            rgba(247, 247, 248, 0.94) 600px,
            rgba(247, 247, 248, 0.55) 900px,
            rgba(247, 247, 248, 0.28) 1300px
          ),
          url("/images/palace.jpg");
        background-repeat: no-repeat;
        background-position: center, center right;
        background-size: cover;
        /* The halftone at full strength competes with the letter; keep the
           whole backdrop at partial strength so the text stays the subject. */
        opacity: 0.55;
      }

      main {
        display: grid;
        gap: 20px;
        justify-items: start;
      }

      .letter,
      .model,
      .members {
        display: grid;
        gap: 20px;
      }

      .member-list {
        list-style: disc;
        padding-left: 2ch;
      }

      .para {
        max-width: 72ch;
      }

      .sep,
      h1,
      .label {
        font-size: inherit;
        font-weight: 400;
      }

      h1,
      .label {
        font-family: "Xanh Mono", ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace;
        font-size: 15px;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      }

      /* Links stay ink-coloured; a grey underline is the only tell. */
      a {
        color: inherit;
        text-decoration: underline;
        text-decoration-color: #a9a9ae;
        text-underline-offset: 3px;
      }

      a:hover {
        text-decoration-color: #111111;
      }

      .cursor {
        animation: blink 1s step-end infinite;
      }

      @keyframes blink {
        50% {
          opacity: 0;
        }
      }

      .signature {
        width: 280px;
        max-width: 100%;
        height: auto;
        margin-top: 20px;
        overflow: visible;
      }

      .sig-ink path {
        fill: #111111;
      }

      /* Sits a hair below the ink so the writing leaves an indent behind it. */
      .sig-ghost {
        transform: translate(0.6px, 1.3px);
      }

      .sig-ghost path {
        fill: #dcdce0;
      }

      /* Wide enough to uncover the full pen width it runs under. */
      .sig-nib {
        fill: none;
        stroke: #ffffff;
        stroke-width: 3.2;
        stroke-linecap: round;
        stroke-linejoin: round;
        stroke-dasharray: 1;
        stroke-dashoffset: 1;
        /* Hidden until its turn, else the round cap uncovers a dot of ink. */
        visibility: hidden;
        animation-name: sig-draw;
        animation-timing-function: linear;
        animation-fill-mode: forwards;
      }

      @keyframes sig-draw {
        from {
          stroke-dashoffset: 1;
          visibility: visible;
        }

        to {
          stroke-dashoffset: 0;
          visibility: visible;
        }
      }

      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .cursor {
          animation: none;
        }

        .sig-nib {
          animation: none;
          stroke-dashoffset: 0;
          visibility: visible;
        }
      }

      /* Narrow screens: the text runs the full width, so keep the palace to a
         faint edge instead of letting it run under the words. */
      @media (max-width: 900px) {
        body::before {
          background-image: linear-gradient(
              to right,
              rgba(247, 247, 248, 0.95) 0%,
              rgba(247, 247, 248, 0.88) 50%,
              rgba(247, 247, 248, 0.7) 78%,
              rgba(247, 247, 248, 0.55) 100%
            ),
            url("/images/palace.jpg");
        }
      }

      @media (max-width: 600px) {
        body {
          padding: 20px;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>MODERN FABER <span class="cursor" aria-hidden="true">_</span></h1>

      <p class="sep" aria-hidden="true">* * *</p>

      <section class="letter" aria-label="To the fabers">
        <p class="label">TO THE FABERS:</p>
        <p class="para">
          Faber is an old word for a maker &mdash; the smith at the forge, the carpenter at the
          bench. <em>Homo faber</em>: the one who makes. There have never been fewer &mdash; not
          for lack of wanting, but because talking about making became easier than making. The
          feed rewards the announcement, not the object, and whole rooms fill with people
          circling the work they say they want to do.
        </p>
        <p class="para">
          Modern Faber is a room for the ones who still make. One rule holds it together: come
          back every week with something real, and say what you changed. No audience, no applause
          &mdash; only other fabers paying attention to the details you almost skipped. That
          attention costs something. It is meant to. Keep the rhythm long enough and you are left
          with a body of work, a sharper eye, and the few people you actually want beside you at
          the bench.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="sep" aria-hidden="true">* * *</p>

      <section class="model" aria-labelledby="model-heading">
        <p class="label" id="model-heading">HOW WE OPERATE:</p>
        <p class="para">
          <strong>ADMISSION.</strong> One thing gets you in: an artifact with taste &mdash; the
          subtle decisions that make you curious who made it. Not a title, not a plan. AI-made is
          fine; raw Claude or Codex is obvious &mdash; what you decide on top of it is not. The
          vote is unanimous, and a single no keeps the door shut.
        </p>
        <p class="para">
          <strong>COMMUNITY.</strong> An open agora &mdash; bring up what you are stuck on, show
          work still rough in the middle. You hold your seat with what you share and what you
          answer.
        </p>
        <p class="para">
          <strong>MEETUPS.</strong> Three or four to a table, never more, matched at random.
          Ninety minutes dense enough that you leave holding something you could not have reached
          alone &mdash; and wanting the next one.
        </p>
      </section>

